3cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "51bb3af5-9e13-5fb9-99b8-bf5b2cb06277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328218/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "efcb9209-e8f0-5f5b-b0dd-08c5d815dcab" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328218/field-4/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-328218/field-4/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328218" :question/id #uuid "146f2d83-686f-5f58-9e04-992ef6d10c3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-328218" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}56 \\\\ -98\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}56 \\\\ -98\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =14\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =14v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=14v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=14.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328218/field-1" "q-328218/field-2" "q-328218/field-3" "q-328218/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328218"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78246/selection/bf4f3604481f35dc66e719ef5275cdee0af50