209facafee9cffa532184dd7efbe10522a0a648f70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78246" :question/id #uuid "ce9fd52a-eff4-5470-8dd1-42e7a1e8d09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78246" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-85 \\\\ -119\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-85 \\\\ -119\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =17\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =17v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=17v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=17.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78246/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78246"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159760/selection/50d85cd6a23d4461be9f78183cc3fc560695e94ba69b13c99654714ddf66e0df" :answer/id #uuid "2bf89fab-6738-5f87-b160-41f9e857fa13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159760/selection/c4709939c2d41bfa5e20b8e347c939c5a6b99255559c2a4a69313e5df4bface5" :answer/id #uuid "70e31f39-5481-5594-b7a7-fdf07cf2add2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159760/selection/02122719f03b5fe1647a171d183ecc1351a6a747cb137a1a65361e8d30cee6b2" :answer/id #uuid "35881203-e684-5a