\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=4v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=4.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328222/field-1" "q-328222/field-2" "q-328222/field-3" "q-328222/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection/f2e35c75509dcf5c71f58acc2ec320ffd57e6703a0860cd24655fbcda54435ac" :answer/id #uuid "cec459f5-195c-5c54-9b15-cd6da891c1a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection/ff8ec718eaf961bbdd855f0e9d0ccd6656986d8f02c4693d1e82ab5f688b2998" :answer/id #uuid "a46eb332-be83-5ff3-a8ae-aadebd540835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection/a5eabde3efdac3395797e1141519f2335dde83a61bd87985071ffb0eefa4c40e" :answer/id #uuid "c23ae6f6-900c-5bd1-8087-ccba66e5857d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection/32f351afbd30a0dca8c93727e45b9ec55b7405cb9d4adebb960f4e92e01644ac" :answer/id #uuid "90ef9595-d847-5979-b71e-b922289814ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection/bdcc335bd77472d2d0d98c64bcf20c5780a9a374367708a77c29b65df644e9ed" :answer/id #uuid "2c352065-6a0b-57d8-84fd-6bc3a2ba0559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9b7365-4078-5822-81fa-131f2d46bfdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78253/selection/bdcc335bd77472d2d0d98c64bcf20c5780a9a374367708a77c29b65df644e9ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-78253/selection/f2e35c75509dcf5c71f58acc2ec320ffd57e6703a0860cd24655fbcda54435ac" "q-78253/selection/ff8ec718eaf961bbdd855f0e9d0ccd6656986d8f02c4693d1e82ab5f688b2998" "q-78253/selection/a5eabde3efdac3395797e1141519f2335dde83a61bd87985071ffb0eefa4c40e" "q-78253/selection/32f351afbd30a0dca8c93727e45b9ec55b7405cb9d4adebb960f4e92e01644ac" "q-78253/selection/bdcc335bd77472d2d0d98c64bcf20c5780a9a374367708a77c29b65df644e9ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78253" :question/id #uuid "9e22d249-389a-52e9-bbc0-d4b4de64dd64" :question/math-academy-id "q-78253" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{3}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection/7b2b2003ad963f68daed9c6ef4b2b763e80129d7116b022d5f708c0e60008827" :answer/id #uuid "3816d20e-19e5-5888-a70c-0dcf36d68d32" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection/4cd9e3e316e375e1a6f86d53664f9f2ba4ff6a1d71402db2e29d15d72e91f8d7" :answer/id #uuid "915e9cf5-f84b-51eb-b1e7-e8e7cfe49532" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection/83351679bef40cdde3e69e55c2c6f08222a317ed82557f1e3ec0abdce5a513f4" :answer/id #uuid "797910a5-edfe-55a1-ab8c-07362f943a1b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection/e83124fc27aa1e0e60220a71689ded676a2d736077007fe067799a7e8888e557" :answer/id #uuid "93db7508-1051-5730-b155-6c24c024cea0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{7}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection/354549e05d30f5acb6c9a5e876a1b220679b1daee3381277145bd16fe273c514" :answer/id #uuid "26b7b347-c6b2-5d74-aac4-2e7a5cc58499" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8087/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b64b693-2979-51cd-91d4-04d9bcbcf76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8087/selection/4cd9e3e316e375e1a6f86d53664f9f2ba4ff6a1d71402db2e29d15d72e91f8d7" :answe